<title>USA: Rayovac says Thomas H. Lee Co  deal closed.</title>
<headline>Rayovac says Thomas H. Lee Co  deal closed.</headline>
<dateline>MADISON, Wis. 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rayovac Corp said it closed a transaction in which Thomas H. Lee Co acquired 80 percent of Rayovac's common stock.</p>
<p>The remaining 20 percent will be owned by Thomas Pyle, Rayovac's former chief executive, and other current and former members of senior management, the company said.</p>
<p>Pyle will remain associated with the company in a consulting capacity, it said. Rayovac makes batteries and flashlights. Lee is a private, Boston-based investment firm.</p>
<p>--Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8787</p>
</text>
